    "etymology": {
     "text": "Phono-semantic compound: semantic 辶 (‘walk’) + phonetic 言. Originally a verb ‘to meet’ (now read yàn); borrowed for ‘this’ through a medieval confusion with 遮 (zhē, ‘this’).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "这 (zhè) ‘this’, 那 (nà) ‘that’ and 哪 (nǎ) ‘which’ form a set: 这里 here, 那里 there, 哪里 where?"
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "Before a noun, 这 normally needs a measure word: 这个西红柿, 这根黄瓜.",
     "Many northerners say zhèi before a measure word: 这个 zhèige."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "As a subject, 这 stands alone: 这是土豆 ‘this is a potato’ — no measure word."
    ]
   },
