    "funFacts": [
     "这 ‘this’, 那 ‘that’ and 哪 ‘which?’ form a family: 这里 / 那里 / 哪里 — here, there, where?"
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "那 nà ‘that’ and 哪 nǎ ‘which?’ differ only in tone and in the 口 of the written form.",
     "Before a noun 那 needs a measure word: 那个人, 那本书 — but alone as a subject it stands bare: 那是老师."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "Many northerners say nèi before a measure word: 那个 nèige (and 这个 zhèige).",
     "At the start of a sentence 那 means ‘well then’: 那好吧 ‘OK then’."
    ]
